<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<loadFolders>

  <!-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Two of the mod's defs carry MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty" -
       the JobDef and the JoyKindDef - so without Royalty they are never created. A DefInjected
       key aimed at a def that does not exist injects into nothing, silently. Their French
       translations therefore have to load only when Royalty does, which is what the Royalty
       folder below is for. The ThoughtDef is NOT gated, so its translation stays at the root
       with the Keyed strings.

       THE ROOT HAS TO BE LISTED. Verified in Verse.ModContentPack.InitLoadFolders: when a
       version block matches, the game adds the folders named here AND RETURNS. Neither the mod
       root nor Common/ is added behind them. Drop the <li>/</li> and the mod loses its Defs,
       its Patches, its assembly and its About in one go.

       A DLC IS A MOD LIKE ANY OTHER HERE. IfModActive ends up in
       ModLister.AnyModActiveNoSuffix, which lowercases the identifier before looking it up, and
       expansions sit in the mod list with a fixed packageId - the same reason MayRequire can
       name Royalty directly. -->

  <v1.6>
    <li>/</li>
    <li IfModActive="Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty">Royalty</li>
  </v1.6>

</loadFolders>
